## 1. Scope

This reference covers heat shrink sleeving for 8.7/15 kV busbars in switchgear and panel builds. Insulating a busbar changes the clearance calculation, so this document is written around the two reasons a builder does it: dielectric withstand and phase spacing.

## 2. Construction

- Cross-linked polyolefin or fluoropolymer based sleeving with anti-tracking fillers.
- Applied over the bar and recovered with hot air, so the sleeve takes the profile of the bar, including bends.
- Heavy wall versions available where the bar is large or the clearance demand is high.
- Available in the colours used to identify phases.

